+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `depres/ranges.py`: implemented `satisfies()` and `max_satisfying()` per `docs/RANGES.md` (`||` sets, primitives, partials/X-ranges, hyphen, tilde, caret, prerelease rule, `ValueError` on invalid range or version). `max_satisfying` returns the original string, and the first one on ties.
+- `tests/test_ranges_spec.py` (new): about 70 cases covering the spec's partial-version table, hyphen/tilde/caret examples, prerelease rules and invalid inputs. No existing test was edited.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` ran 12 tests, all OK. That includes every test in `tests/test_ranges.py`.
+
+## Not verified / unsure
+- Behaviour the doc doesn't specify, which I chose to match npm:
+  - `>*` and `<*` match nothing.
+  - An empty `||` branch (e.g. `"1.x || "`) matches everything, per the "empty set" rule.
+  - Spaced operators like `~ 1.2.3` are accepted.
+- Prerelease on a partial (e.g. `1.x-beta`) is rejected as invalid.
+- I did not run the resolver itself or CI, and did not compare against the npm `semver` package.
